{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "PortIO Port Registry API",
    "description": "PortIO is the **local development port authority** for this Mac. Many projects run at once (frontends, Firebase emulators, APIs, PM2 processes). They must not share the same TCP ports — conflicts cause flaky startups, wrong apps answering, and hard-to-debug failures.\n\n## Why you are here\n\nIf you are an agent or another platform setting up (or retargeting) a project's local ports, **do not invent port numbers**. Ask PortIO first, claim what you need, then write those numbers into the project (dev scripts, emulator config, and `.webfootprint/ports.json`).\n\nDashboard UI: `http://localhost:3850` · This API / Swagger: `http://127.0.0.1:3853`\n\n## Two complementary sources of truth\n\n1. **This registry (claims)** — reservations for ports you are about to use. Persisted on disk by the PortIO daemon. Use `GET /api/ports/next` to suggest free ports, then `POST /api/ports/claim` to reserve them.\n2. **Per-project `.webfootprint/ports.json`** (or legacy `wf-ports.json`) — what PortIO monitors on the dashboard (live status, kill buttons, export/duplicates). Claiming via this API does **not** rewrite that file; update it after you claim.\n\nThere is **no Firebase / remote DB** in PortIO. Live UI state is in-memory over WebSocket; claims alone are persisted locally.\n\n## What counts as \"taken\"\n\nWhen suggesting or claiming, PortIO excludes:\n- Always-blocked ports (entire `0–1023` plus common services like MySQL/Redis/AirPlay/8080 — see `GET /api/ports/blocked`)\n- Ports already declared in any scanned project's `ports.json`\n- Ports already claimed in this registry\n- Ports currently listening on the machine (`lsof`)\n\n## Recommended workflow for another project\n\n1. `GET /api/ports/conflicts` — see existing duplicate declarations (fix those first if your project is listed).\n2. `GET /api/ports` or `GET /api/ports/next?count=N&from=4000` — learn what is free.\n3. `POST /api/ports/claim` with `{ \"projectId\": \"<your-project-id>\", \"service\": \"Frontend\", \"count\": N }` (or a specific `\"port\"`).\n4. Put the returned ports into your app config **and** into `<project>/.webfootprint/ports.json` so PortIO can monitor them.\n5. `DELETE /api/ports/claim/{port}` only if you abandon a reservation you no longer need.\n\n## Quick examples\n\n```bash\n# Suggest 3 free ports starting at 4000\ncurl 'http://127.0.0.1:3853/api/ports/next?count=3&from=4000'\n\n# Claim them for your project\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:3853/api/ports/claim \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"projectId\":\"my-app\",\"service\":\"Frontend\",\"count\":1,\"from\":4000}'\n```\n\nConflict responses return **409** when the requested port is blocked, declared, claimed, or already listening.",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:3853",
      "description": "Local portio-daemon"
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/ports": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "List all known ports",
        "description": "Union of declared project ports, registry claims, curated blocked ports, and currently listening ports.",
        "operationId": "listPorts",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Port inventory",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "ports": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PortEntry" }
                    },
                    "blockedRange": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "properties": {
                        "from": { "type": "integer" },
                        "to": { "type": "integer" }
                      }
                    },
                    "claims": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Claim" }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/ports/conflicts": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "List declared port conflicts",
        "operationId": "listConflicts",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Ports declared by more than one project/service",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "duplicatePorts": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "port": { "type": "integer" },
                          "usedBy": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "items": {
                              "type": "object",
                              "properties": {
                                "project": { "type": "string" },
                                "service": { "type": "string" }
                              }
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/ports/blocked": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "List always-unavailable ports",
        "operationId": "listBlocked",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "System range plus curated blocked ports",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "systemRange": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "properties": {
                        "from": { "type": "integer" },
                        "to": { "type": "integer" }
                      }
                    },
                    "systemHighlights": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "port": { "type": "integer" },
                          "label": { "type": "string" }
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "ports": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "port": { "type": "integer" },
                          "label": { "type": "string" },
                          "source": { "type": "string" }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/ports/next": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Suggest free port(s) without claiming",
        "operationId": "suggestNext",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "count",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": { "type": "integer", "default": 1, "minimum": 1, "maximum": 50 }
          },
          {
            "name": "from",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": { "type": "integer", "default": 4000, "minimum": 1, "maximum": 65535 }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Suggested free ports",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "ports": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": { "type": "integer" }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": { "description": "No free ports found in range" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/ports/claim": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Claim a port (specific or auto-allocate)",
        "operationId": "claimPort",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ClaimRequest" }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Claim created",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "claims": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Claim" }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": { "description": "Missing projectId or bad request" },
          "409": { "description": "Requested port unavailable" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/ports/claim/{port}": {
      "delete": {
        "summary": "Release a claim",
        "operationId": "releaseClaim",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "port",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": { "type": "integer" }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Claim released",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "port": { "type": "integer" }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": { "description": "No claim for that port" }
        }
      }
    },
    "/docs": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "PortIO reference documentation (markdown)",
        "description": "Static integration instructions for other projects, agents and scripts: port registry workflow, command API, WebSocket topics, and the `.webfootprint` config formats. Served instantly, independent of the project scan. Also available as `/docs.md`, and as `http://localhost:3850/help.md` via the dashboard dev server.",
        "operationId": "getDocs",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Markdown document",
            "content": {
              "text/markdown": { "schema": { "type": "string" } }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/docs.json": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "PortIO reference documentation (JSON envelope)",
        "operationId": "getDocsJson",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Markdown wrapped in JSON",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": { "type": "boolean" },
                    "markdown": { "type": "string" }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "Claim": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "port": { "type": "integer" },
          "projectId": { "type": "string" },
          "service": { "type": "string", "nullable": true },
          "claimedAt": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
        }
      },
      "ClaimRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["projectId"],
        "properties": {
          "projectId": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Project id that will use the port"
          },
          "service": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Optional service name (e.g. Frontend)"
          },
          "port": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Specific port to claim; omit to auto-allocate"
          },
          "count": {
            "type": "integer",
            "default": 1,
            "description": "How many ports to auto-allocate when port is omitted"
          },
          "from": {
            "type": "integer",
            "default": 4000,
            "description": "Start scanning from this port when auto-allocating"
          }
        }
      },
      "PortEntry": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "port": { "type": "integer" },
          "source": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": ["declared", "claimed", "blocked", "listening"]
          },
          "label": { "type": "string" },
          "usedBy": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "object" } },
          "claim": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Claim" },
          "listening": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "pid": { "type": "integer" },
              "command": { "type": "string" }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
